+## Intended correction
 
-V9.9.5 changes runtime ownership/topology while keeping recovered map timing/route code unchanged. One dedicated minimap-only `main_farm_worker` owns farm cadence for every recovered Spotify profile. The full-screen supervisor is kept for preview/UI/alerts/MiuMiu and is FPS-paced so it cannot become the cadence source. The final parity revision also scopes Nghia's two-frame minimap outlier extension back to C2, matching its V9.9.4 ownership instead of applying it to every profile.
+This pass corrects one forensic mapping error before stable publication. The final Spotify Offline V4 re-audit shows `Farm.left_and_right` importing/calling the shared `hold_combo_action` and does not show `perform_dynamic_combo` in that Farm module cluster. The previous candidate overreached by routing map C2 directly to the separate Dynamic Combo SPAM timing block.
+
+## Hot helper correction
+
+- C1, C2, B1 and B3 all remain SIMPLE and now share `_spotify_hold_combo_action`.
+- The C2-only routing branch to `_spotify_c2_tp_skill_hold_combo` was removed from `_spotify_primary_skill_step`.
+- `_spotify_c2_tp_skill_hold_combo` is retained only as a dormant representation of the separate Dynamic Combo SPAM facility so its real `20..50 ms` / `0.05..0.15 s` evidence is not lost.
+- Shared `hold_combo_action` no longer sleeps `0.015..0.045 s` between Flash and Skill or `0.125..0.255 s` after Skill. Those ranges are now explicitly documented as `random_move` timing only.
+- Shared Flash and Skill taps use the direct global `ATTACK_HOLD_MIN/MAX = 50..150 ms`. This is the strongest current structural hypothesis, not a claim of exact Python-source recovery.
 
 ## Preserved behavior
 
-- C1/B1/B3 continue to dispatch through the recovered `LEFT_RIGHT`/`run_left_and_right` path.
-- C2 continues to use the V9.9.4 TP+Skill helper and cached-focus abort behavior.
-- Bunny, Stand Still, Pirate2 and Pirate2 1-Hit continue through their existing dedicated recovered routes.
-- Recovered timing catalog values and `spotify_recovered_core.py` are byte-identical to V9.9.4.
-- Focus parity, MiuMiu, PC Alarm, maps.json and the Spotify dispatcher are byte-identical to V9.9.4.
-- Main-farm stages remain `STATE -> SELL_SAFE -> PET -> RECOVERY -> BUFF1 -> BUFF2 -> DISPATCH`.
-- Sell handoff still places the pause gate before spawning the asynchronous seller.
-
-## Position parity correction
-
-- V9.9.4 used `_c2_fast_observe_position()` only inside the C2 fast worker.
-- The first V9.9.5 worker generalization unintentionally reused that outlier guard for every profile.
-- The corrected V9.9.5 worker accepts detected positions immediately for C1/B1/B3, Bunny, Stand Still/C1 Stand Still, Pirate2 and Pirate2 1-Hit.
-- C2 keeps the existing two-frame outlier guard as a Nghia stability extension; no C2 attack timing was changed.
-- Regression coverage explicitly tests all eight non-C2 profile names plus C2 two-frame confirmation.
-
-## Ownership/safety review
-
-- Exact Spotify profiles have one farm owner: `Nghia-Spotify-MainFarm`.
-- The worker hot loop consumes cached HWND state and contains no direct window enumeration or full-screen capture.
-- Preview-only, sell lock, pause reason, unsupported profile, non-parity mode, missing cached HWND and worker exception all fail safe by releasing owned input.
-- Supervisor does not call `spotify_main_farm_orchestrator.tick()`.
-- If the worker is not alive, the supervisor may detect position for preview/context but does not regain farm ownership.
-- STOP invalidates the worker generation before behavior-engine shutdown.
