+- Cached-focus worker architecture is unchanged; no direct EnumWindows/window lookup was reintroduced to the farm hot path.
+- C2's two-frame minimap outlier extension remains C2-only.
+- Bunny, Stand Still, Pirate2 and Pirate2 1-Hit route logic is unchanged.
+- `spotify_timing_catalog.py`, `spotify_behavior_engine.py`, `spotify_recovered_api.py`, `spotify_focus_parity.py`, MiuMiu, PC Alarm and `maps.json` remain byte-identical to the prior corrected V9.9.5 candidate.
+- Dynamic Combo SPAM remains available as a separate recovered API facility but is not inferred from the C2 map name.
+
+## Validation
+
+- New hot-helper tests were observed RED on the previous candidate and GREEN after the minimal correction.
+- Full local suite: 43/43 PASS.
+- `compileall`: PASS.
+- `spotify_recovered_core.py` SHA-256: `18e164944d5842629af55ca0f70f274192421515c01ac6451c0bdedf13109d95`.
+- `maple_nghia_pro.py` SHA-256 remains `8ee70b2b457dd21010f3adbeb30dbb7052245d846304295fddd59290c8f9ba48`.
+- Reference Spotify `main.dll` SHA-256: `62860aeb8a80ac4a768aa8f3afafe23f079aa07e2981786e44989ad71b941cb0`.
 
 ## Validation boundary
 
-40 local pytest cases and compileall validate code structure and regressions. They are not a same-machine runtime A/B measurement against Spotify, and they are not a substitute for the Windows/Nuitka build + launcher smoke required before stable publication.
+This source correction is structurally better grounded than the previous C2-special candidate, but the exact shared inner hold distribution remains unresolved at source level. The 50..150 ms inner hold uses direct global Spotify constants plus helper shape and observed cadence as evidence. A fresh Windows/Nuitka build + launcher smoke and same-machine runtime A/B are still required before stable publication.
